{"lines":[{"t":"Reading","y":0.035467374403211571,"w":0.085256029764811281,"h":0.021981280880625897,"c":1,"x":0.83410914815939496},{"c":1,"y":0.0797921861443599,"x":0.077966497322207909,"w":0.79669118245442705,"h":0.022670714397452829,"t":"for example, by looking back at the light that penetrated through the tunnel mouth, and made"},{"t":"corrections whenever necessary. Large deviations could happen, and they could result in one end","y":0.098042407276431209,"h":0.021652732777230455,"x":0.078032524314244442,"c":1,"w":0.8274775187174479},{"w":0.81736195882161455,"c":1,"h":0.023957356968532628,"t":"of the tunnel not being usable. An inscription written on the side of a 428-meter tunnel, built by","x":0.077948955768636197,"y":0.11423902029201616},{"x":0.075930474337483442,"y":0.13318500815593115,"w":0.82959660847981764,"h":0.022998351511601345,"c":1,"t":"the Romans as part of the Saldae aqueduct system in modern-day Algeria, describes how the two"},{"c":1,"x":0.0759220159488109,"h":0.02157407542701606,"y":0.15021749279664598,"t":"teams of builders missed each other in the mountain and how the later construction of a lateral","w":0.80907267252604165},{"x":0.07585899849667968,"w":0.46359644571940106,"y":0.1658999055607101,"t":"link between both corridors corrected the initial error.","h":0.021711878557508446,"c":1},{"t":"The Romans dug tunnels for their roads using the counter-excavation method, whenever they","w":0.79471750895182292,"x":0.075891287449872488,"c":1,"h":0.024274021773231569,"y":0.20303716782063308},{"y":0.21816027790921078,"c":1,"x":0.075865030551561477,"h":0.027370637100633144,"w":0.77019419352213547,"t":"encountered obstacles such as hills or mountains that were too high for roads to pass over."},{"y":0.2402317805052554,"w":0.80075246175130199,"h":0.021466642723487972,"x":0.07596684803258863,"c":1,"t":"An example is the 37-meter-long, 6-meter-high, Furlo Pass Tunnel built in Italy in 69-79 CE."},{"h":0.020931969542666296,"c":1,"t":"Remarkably, a modern road still uses this tunnel today. Tunnels were also built for mineral","x":0.075976093834694891,"w":0.77189193725585947,"y":0.25829760156918802},{"t":"extraction. Miners would locate a mineral vein and then pursue it with shafts and tunnels","x":0.075924058650199133,"y":0.27536198914889787,"w":0.75965535481770829,"h":0.023229160915415159,"c":1},{"t":"underground. Traces of such tunnels used to mine gold can still be found at the Dolaucothi mines","y":0.29339905546387335,"c":1,"h":0.021474810174553327,"x":0.073932488060209592,"w":0.83364232381184911},{"w":0.8091186014811198,"h":0.023951394538295423,"x":0.07380008249961785,"c":1,"t":"in Wales. When the sole purpose of a tunnel was mineral extraction, construction required less","y":0.31076968904352364},{"y":0.32793369303714004,"c":1,"h":0.022402817284681742,"x":0.073850254736235008,"w":0.56426905314127607,"t":"planning, as the tunnel route was determined by the mineral vein."},{"x":0.073902403824604709,"w":0.78015813191731775,"c":1,"t":"Roman tunnel projects were carefully planned and carried out. The length of time it took to","y":0.36415477858977319,"h":0.020672888020042635},{"w":0.82962331136067713,"y":0.38129348601561364,"c":1,"x":0.071827372256338146,"h":0.023579463801479461,"t":"construct a tunnel depended on the method being used and the type of rock being excavated. The"},{"w":0.82946507771809896,"x":0.071907184769779059,"h":0.019508395515145383,"c":1,"y":0.40007164366362757,"t":"ganat construction method was usually faster than the counter-excavation method as it was more"},{"y":0.41659900124436622,"c":1,"h":0.022005779863948471,"t":"straightforward. This was because the mountain could be excavated not only from the tunnel","w":0.79256642659505205,"x":0.07183033396376895},{"t":"mouths but also from shafts. The type of rock could also influence construction times. When","y":0.43490420062807067,"w":0.79255579630533857,"x":0.071829147059371698,"h":0.022628449438879206,"c":1},{"y":0.45262513948574512,"t":"the rock was hard, the Romans employed a technique called fire quenching which consisted of","x":0.071805714352225034,"w":0.80900955200195301,"h":0.023010337029806371,"c":1},{"x":0.07175588601270666,"w":0.80296712239583334,"t":"heating the rock with fire, and then suddenly cooling it with cold water so that it would crack.","c":1,"y":0.47023939017033944,"h":0.023141690221635924},{"w":0.79052103678385433,"t":"Progress through hard rock could be very slow, and it was not uncommon for tunnels to take","h":0.023037985721943155,"y":0.48829072184392364,"c":1,"x":0.071800999716371341},{"h":0.02323941768830462,"t":"years, if not decades, to be built. Construction marks left on a Roman tunnel in Bologna show that","c":1,"x":0.06978493997600424,"y":0.50638985811639836,"w":0.84395248413085944},{"h":0.022106044845670914,"t":"the rate of advance through solid rock was 30 centimeters per day. In contrast, the rate of advance","w":0.83576532999674469,"y":0.52410571939397266,"c":1,"x":0.069768054196945761},{"y":0.54200490905765508,"w":0.79044962565104171,"t":"of the Claudius tunnel can be calculated at 1.4 meters per day. Most tunnels had inscriptions","x":0.069803385880304436,"h":0.022265922896853585,"c":1},{"t":"showing the names of patrons who ordered construction and sometimes the name of the architect.","x":0.069790044908902574,"h":0.022454240437250417,"y":0.55920789654144287,"w":0.83577219645182277,"c":1},{"t":"For example, the 1.4-kilometer Çevlik tunnel in Turkey, built to divert the floodwater threatening","c":1,"y":0.57694459856589619,"x":0.06973524879117321,"w":0.82761678059895827,"h":0.024270791187443685},{"t":"the harbor of the ancient city of Seleuceia Pieria, had inscriptions on the entrance, still visible","y":0.59401344168547054,"x":0.069717119637250469,"w":0.80292134602864595,"h":0.024617641076041918,"c":1},{"t":"today, that also indicate that the tunnel was started in 69 CE and was completed in 81 CE.","x":0.067757637601676871,"h":0.021894881806749922,"c":1,"y":0.61254760330634528,"w":0.77192230224609382},{"x":0.87860082314842769,"y":0.91133720913026606,"t":"83","w":0.024691357612609877,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","y":0.95609090412250985,"w":0.25054743448893235,"h":0.027841228759190484,"c":1,"x":0.71929884506155906}],"h":3396,"w":2400}